# Build context of the fixed Dockerfile (read by BuildKit only, which takes it
# over any .dockerignore at the root). Protected file (.gitea/**).
# Never leak a secret or an unnecessary file into an image layer: only what
# the tool needs at runtime is copied.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.git
# Every node_modules, at any depth: a committed node_modules/ would be copied
# over the installed dependencies and preferred by Node's resolution.
**/node_modules

# Files pnpm reads or executes: forbidden in the repository, and kept out of
# the build in any case — except the root pnpm-workspace.yaml, the platform's
# own (protected) pnpm settings, read by the fixed Dockerfile's install.
**/.pnpmfile.*
**/.npmrc
**/pnpm-workspace.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml

# Agent rules, CI, analysis rules and documentation: not needed at runtime.
.claude/
agents/
AGENTS.md
AGENTS.fr.md
CLAUDE.md
.gitea/
.opengrep/
design/
docs/
scripts/
README.md
**/Dockerfile
**/.dockerignore

# Tests.
test/
tests/
**/*.test.js
**/__tests__/
